<div class="legal-document" id="company-privacy-policy">
  <h1 class="legal-document-title">Company Userscript Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-document-subtitle">Last updated: <%= Date.today.strftime("%d %B %Y") %></p>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-introduction">Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Bram, the creator of TornManager. This Privacy Policy covers the <strong>TornManager Company
      userscript</strong>. That is the script you install in a userscript manager (such as Tampermonkey) or in
      Torn PDA. It runs on Torn.com pages and helps company directors see how their company is doing over time.
    </p>
    <p>
      The web platform, the Chats userscript and the Recruiter userscript have their own documents above on this
      page. If you only use the Company userscript, this document and the
      <a href="#company-terms-of-service">Company Terms of Service</a> are the ones that apply to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-information-i-collect">Information I Collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you sign in you provide a <strong>Torn API key with Limited access</strong>. Only Limited keys, or
      Custom keys with company access, are accepted, and only from players who are the director of a company.
      The key is checked with the official Torn API and then <strong>stored on the TornManager server, encrypted</strong>.
      After sign in your browser holds a session token and uses it for every later request. Your API key is not
      sent again by the browser.
    </p>
    <p>On the server, a Company account consists of:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your Torn ID, player name, level and the ID of the company you direct</li>
      <li>Your Torn API key, encrypted</li>
      <li>A daily copy of your company data: the company profile (income, customers, staff, stars), your
        employees (positions, working stats, wages, effectiveness, last action), stock and sales, and company
        details such as funds, popularity, efficiency, environment and trains</li>
      <li>Your company news</li>
      <li>Xanax payments sent for subscriptions, and subscription expiration dates</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your company data includes information about your employees, such as their names, working stats and
      wages. This is the same information Torn shows you as their director. It is only shown to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-torn-api">Calls to the Torn API</h2>
    <p>
      Once a day, and when you ask for a refresh (at most every 15 minutes), the TornManager server uses your
      key to read your own company from the official Torn API. It never uses your key for anything else, never
      shares it, and never adds it to any shared key pool. Every call carries the comment <code>tmcompany</code>,
      so you can see exactly what your key was used for in your own Torn key log.
    </p>
    <p>
      To compare your company with others, the server also stores the public daily company listing that Torn
      publishes for every company. That listing is fetched with TornManager's own keys, not yours.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your key stops working, or you are no longer a director, the server stops using it. A key that Torn
      reports as invalid is deleted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-local-storage">Data Stored in Your Browser</h2>
    <p>The Company userscript stores the following in your browser's localStorage on the torn.com domain:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>User profile and session token</strong> (<code>tc_user</code>): your Torn ID, name and the session token. Cleared when you sign out.</li>
      <li><strong>Company</strong> (<code>tc_company</code>): the name, type and ID of your company.</li>
      <li><strong>Subscription state</strong> (<code>tc_subscription</code>): the last known subscription status.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-backend">Backend Communication</h2>
    <p>
      The Company userscript only talks to tornmanager.com, using <code>GM.xmlHttpRequest</code>: signing in,
      checking your subscription, and loading your company overview, history and news. Nothing is shared with any
      third party.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-retention">Data Retention &amp; Removal</h2>
    <p>
      Your company history is kept while you use the script, so you can see how your company does over months.
      The public company listing of companies nobody tracks is kept for 90 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Remove API key</strong> in the script's settings deletes your key from the server right away and
      stops all daily reads. Deleting or regenerating the key on Torn.com does the same. To also delete your
      stored company history, contact me on Torn:
      <%= link_to "Bram [2728237]", "https://www.torn.com/profiles.php?XID=2728237", target: "_blank", class: "player-link" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-data-security">Data Security &amp; Location</h2>
    <p>
      All communication with tornmanager.com uses secure HTTPS connections. API keys are encrypted in the
      database. Server data is stored in <strong>Helsinki, Finland</strong> (EU) within the Hetzner datacenter,
      which means your data falls under European Union data protection laws, including GDPR. No method of
      transmission or storage is 100% secure. I work hard to protect your data, but I cannot guarantee absolute
      security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-age-requirement">Age Requirement</h2>
    <p>
      In line with Torn's Terms of Service, you must be at least 13 years old to use the Company userscript.
      I do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-changes">Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      I may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes are shown by updating the
      "Last updated" date at the top. If you keep using the Company userscript after changes, you accept the
      updated policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="cpp-contact">Contact Me</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how I handle your data, please reach out to me on Torn:
    </p>
    <p>
      <%= link_to "Bram [2728237]", "https://www.torn.com/profiles.php?XID=2728237", target: "_blank", class: "player-link" %>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
